; A GENERIC INSTANTIATION used as a bare member/element type (`[pair<uint, tstr>]`) is SUPPORTED:
; the group-entry `TypeGroupname` arm routes through the shared `generic_instance_or_new_type` helper
; (parsing.rs), registering the anonymous instance (`PairU64Text`) exactly like keyed members,
; rule RHSes, and homogeneous array elements. This fixture pins that the member position generates
; cleanly (regression guard against the arm reverting to its old `todo!()`). Round-trip execution of
; the shape lives in tests/corpus/generic_call_member.cddl; the boundary neighbours (arity mismatch,
; undefined generic, generics on plain groups) are pinned by their own robustness/matrix fixtures.
; Surfaced originally by the recombination sweep (src/tests/recombination_tests.rs).
pair<k, v> = [k, v]
a = [pair<uint, tstr>]
